_id\n) oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY 1;\n\nBut date_trunc returns timestamp. Rule month default DATE_TRUNC. Fine. Could name month. Need only orders with items handled by inner join. If order item order has no matching orders? Usually all. Need month from orders. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"有商品明细的订单等权\" means each order with item detail equal weight. The join and avg order totals gives equal order weight. Good.\n\nNeed no code fences. Output SQL only. Could include comment? Not necessary. Need LIMIT? Query grouped by month, no explicit LIMIT rule says must LIMIT except aggregate one row. We need LIMIT. Since group by months maybe many rows. Rule 3 must LIMIT. Add LIMIT maybe 100? TopN? But question asks each month. Yet hard rule says must LIMIT. We can LIMIT 1000 maybe. Need not alter? Add LIMIT maybe 10000? Data max ~25 months, limit 100 safe. The rule says must LIMIT. Use LIMIT 100. But if each month beyond 100? Dataset only 2016-2018, <=27. Fine. Need maybe no limit? Hard rule. Add LIMIT 100. Need not order? For each month, time ascending by group shape rule. ORDER BY month. Limit after order. Good.\n\nNeed check use ROUND(AVG(oi.order_total), 2) if AVG numeric returns numeric, okay.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"明细商品金额合计\" = sum(price) not including freight. Yes order_items.price. Good.\n\nNeed output month maybe \"month\". Average amount.\n\nNeed no explanation. final SQL.\n\nLet's ensure SQL valid with alias month maybe \"month\" reserved? In PostgreSQL month is not reserved? Could use order_month. Better. Query:\n\nSELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS order_month,\n       ROUND(AVG(oi.order_total), 2) AS avg_order_amount\nFROM orders o\nJOIN (\n    SELECT order_id, SUM(price) AS order_total\n    FROM order_items\n    GROUP BY order_id\n) oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\nGROUP BY DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp)\nORDER BY order_month\nLIMIT 100;\n\nNeed maybe date_trunc timestamp no timezone. Fine.\n\nNeed m